// SR 632.10 — Section 8 Final Provisions
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
Originally Section 7. The original Arts. 12–15 became Arts. 14–17.
|

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 14 Economic Policy Commission
The Federal Council shall appoint an Economic Policy Commission as an advisory body.
|

:NOTE
Art. 14 — Amended by No I 1 of the O of 9 Dec. 2022 on the Amendment of Legislation as a Consequence of the Review of Extra-Parliamentary Commissions, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2022 843).
|

:INFO
Art. 15 Implementation
1 The Federal Council is responsible for implementation. It shall enact the required transitional provisions.
2 The Federal Office for Customs and Border Security shall publish the Working Tariff.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — Amended by No I 17 of the O of 12 June 2020 on the Amendment of Legislation as a consequence of the Change in the Name of the Federal Customs Administration as part of its further Development, in force since 1 Jan. 2022 (AS 2020 2743).
|

:INFO
Art. 16 Amendment and repeal of previous legislation
1 The Federal Council shall revise the provisions of federal legislation that contain tariff headings in accordance with the General Tariff in this Act and shall bring the revised provisions into force at the same time as this Act.
2 The Customs Tariff Act of 19 June 1959 is repealed.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — [AS 1959 1343]
|

:INFO
Art. 17 Referendum and commencement
1 This Act is subject to an optional referendum.
2 The Federal Council shall determine the date on which this Act comes into force.
Commencement Date: 1 January 1988
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — Art. 1 of the O of 4 Nov. 1987 (AS 1987 2309).

